#!/bin/bash
# InfiniBot Desktop AppImage entry point. scripts/appimage-finalize.mjs puts this in
# place of electron-builder's AppRun (which never adds sandbox flags itself,
# while its .desktop entry blindly passed --no-sandbox).
#
# Chromium sandbox on Linux, in the order Chromium itself tries them:
#   1. user-namespace sandbox  - needs unprivileged user namespaces WITH
#      capabilities. Ubuntu 23.10+/24.04 restrict these through AppArmor
#      (kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1) unless an AppArmor
#      profile for the binary allows `userns`; an AppImage cannot install one
#      without root.
#   2. setuid helper (chrome-sandbox root:root 4755) - impossible inside an
#      AppImage: the FUSE mount is nosuid and the files belong to the user.
# When neither works Chromium aborts with
#   FATAL:setuid_sandbox_host.cc ... chrome-sandbox is owned by root and has mode 4755
# so ONLY in that case this script adds --no-sandbox and says so (stderr +
# ~/.config/InfiniBot/launcher.log). Windows keep contextIsolation on,
# nodeIntegration off, and remote cloud windows get no Node bridge.
# The .deb keeps the full sandbox (setuid helper + AppArmor profile).
#
# Environment:
#   INFINIBOT_SANDBOX=force             never add --no-sandbox (Chromium aborts if no sandbox works)
#   INFINIBOT_NO_DESKTOP_INTEGRATION=1  don't add the per-user menu entry/icon

set -u

if [ -z "${APPDIR:-}" ]; then
  APPDIR="$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")"
fi
BIN="$APPDIR/infinibot-desktop"

export PATH="$APPDIR:$APPDIR/usr/sbin:$PATH"
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$APPDIR/usr/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
export XDG_DATA_DIRS="$APPDIR/usr/share/:${XDG_DATA_DIRS:-/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/}"
export GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR="$APPDIR/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas${GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR:+:$GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR}"

CONFIG_DIR="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/InfiniBot"
LOG_FILE="$CONFIG_DIR/launcher.log"

log() {
  echo "[infinibot] $*" >&2
  if mkdir -p "$CONFIG_DIR" 2>/dev/null; then
    # keep the log small
    if [ -f "$LOG_FILE" ] && [ "$(wc -c <"$LOG_FILE" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)" -gt 65536 ]; then
      tail -n 200 "$LOG_FILE" >"$LOG_FILE.tmp" 2>/dev/null && mv -f "$LOG_FILE.tmp" "$LOG_FILE"
    fi
    echo "$(date -Is 2>/dev/null || date) $*" >>"$LOG_FILE" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
}

# Can this process create a user namespace AND act as root inside it (map
# its uid)? That is what Chromium's namespace sandbox needs. Under Ubuntu's
# AppArmor restriction creating the namespace succeeds but the uid_map write
# is denied, which is exactly what this probe catches.
userns_sandbox_ok() {
  [ -e /proc/self/ns/user ] || return 1
  [ "$(cat /proc/sys/user/max_user_namespaces 2>/dev/null || echo 1)" != "0" ] || return 1
  [ "$(cat /proc/sys/kernel/unprivileged_userns_clone 2>/dev/null || echo 1)" = "1" ] || return 1
  if command -v unshare >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    unshare --user --map-root-user /bin/true >/dev/null 2>&1
    return $?
  fi
  # No unshare (very minimal systems): judge by the AppArmor switch.
  [ "$(cat /proc/sys/kernel/apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns 2>/dev/null || echo 0)" != "1" ]
}

# Is the setuid helper usable (root-owned, setuid, on a mount that honours it)?
suid_helper_ok() {
  local helper="$APPDIR/chrome-sandbox"
  [ -u "$helper" ] || return 1
  [ "$(stat -c %u "$helper" 2>/dev/null)" = "0" ] || return 1
  if command -v findmnt >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    findmnt -n -o OPTIONS -T "$helper" 2>/dev/null | tr ',' '\n' | grep -qx nosuid && return 1
  fi
  return 0
}

has_arg() {
  local want="$1"; shift
  local a
  for a in "$@"; do [ "$a" = "$want" ] && return 0; done
  return 1
}

# Per-user menu entry + icon so the AppImage shows up in the app launcher and
# the dock groups its window (StartupWMClass). Skipped when the .deb is
# installed (it has its own entry) or when opted out.
desktop_integration() {
  [ -n "${APPIMAGE:-}" ] || return 0
  [ "${INFINIBOT_NO_DESKTOP_INTEGRATION:-}" = "1" ] && return 0
  [ -f /usr/share/applications/infinibot-desktop.desktop ] && return 0
  case "$APPIMAGE" in *'"'*|*'`'*|*'$'*|*'\'*|*'%'*) return 0 ;; esac
  local data="${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}"
  local entry="$data/applications/infinibot-appimage.desktop"
  local icon_dir="$data/icons/hicolor/512x512/apps"
  local want
  want="[Desktop Entry]
Name=InfiniBot
Comment=Your AI agent team — local gateway and control center
Exec=\"$APPIMAGE\" %U
TryExec=$APPIMAGE
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Icon=infinibot-appimage
StartupWMClass=InfiniBot
Categories=Development;Utility;Network;
X-InfiniBot-AppImage=1"
  if [ ! -f "$entry" ] || [ "$(cat "$entry" 2>/dev/null)" != "$want" ]; then
    mkdir -p "$data/applications" "$icon_dir" 2>/dev/null || return 0
    cp -f "$APPDIR/usr/share/icons/hicolor/512x512/apps/infinibot-desktop.png" "$icon_dir/infinibot-appimage.png" 2>/dev/null || true
    printf '%s\n' "$want" >"$entry" 2>/dev/null || return 0
    command -v update-desktop-database >/dev/null 2>&1 && update-desktop-database -q "$data/applications" >/dev/null 2>&1
    log "menu entry written: $entry"
  fi
  return 0
}

desktop_integration

extra=()
if has_arg --no-sandbox "$@"; then
  :
elif [ "${INFINIBOT_SANDBOX:-auto}" = "force" ]; then
  :
elif userns_sandbox_ok; then
  :
elif suid_helper_ok; then
  :
else
  extra=(--no-sandbox)
  log "Chromium sandbox unavailable here (user namespaces restricted, e.g. Ubuntu 24.04 AppArmor; setuid helper unusable inside an AppImage): starting with --no-sandbox. For the full sandbox install the .deb (Ubuntu/Debian)."
fi

exec "$BIN" ${extra[@]+"${extra[@]}"} "$@"
